<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Hudaco half year share rises 8 percent.</title>
<headline>Hudaco half year share rises 8 percent.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended May 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - headline		80.0	  vs 74.0</p>
<p>    Distribution (cts)    35.5	  vs 33.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   23.8	  vs 17.4</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   38.8	  vs 30.5</p>
<p>    Tax			 10.8	  vs 9.8</p>
<p>    Net finance costs     9.9	   vs 7.7</p>
<p>    Turnover		  568.2	 vs 525.9</p>
<p>    Exceptional items     nil	   vs 4.4 loss</p>
<p>    Outside shareholders  4.2	   vs 3.3</p>
<p>Div payable August 18</p>
<p>on register July 18</p>
<p>Full name: Hudaco Industries Ltd (engineering)</p>
<p>NOTE - South African automotive parts to engineering firm Hudaco Ltd said in a statement that it was uncertain about trading conditions for the rest of the financial year due to an unexpected decline in first quarter GDP.</p>
<p>The firm said reducing expenses and working capital levels would become a priority and it would be disappointed if its second half performance did not match the first half in percentage improvement of earnings per share.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
